Package: rav-audio
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: jch.pallier <jch.pallier@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS@, mpd (>= 0.24), pipewire, pipewire-bin, wireplumber, libspa-0.2-bluetooth, bluez, bluez-tools, systemd
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core, polkitd
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: MPD player with a physical front panel and dual OLED displays
 Turns a Raspberry Pi into a network music player with a front panel: a
 rotary knob and four buttons drive MPD (playback, volume, queue and a
 library browser on the panels), or the connected phone over AVRCP. MPD
 and Bluetooth A2DP play through PipeWire (running as user mpd), and the
 two OLED panels show live visualizations of the output's monitor.
 .
 Panels (display = ... in /etc/rav-audio/visualizer.conf): SSD1309
 128x64 monochrome or SSD1322 240x128 greyscale.
 .
 Output: an I2S DAC such as a HifiBerry when its overlay is enabled,
 otherwise the onboard headphone jack (dtparam=audio=on). Needs
 dtparam=spi=on for the panels.
